&& SYSCMD_EXPORT_MIRROR_v1.dts
&&
&& Export the LIVE SYSCMD table to CSV so the tracked CSV mirrors the canonical
&& table. This is an EXPORT, not an import. The table is authority; the CSV is
&& its readable shadow.
&&
&& WHY THIS DIRECTION, EMPHATICALLY
&&   stack_audit reports CSV_VS_TABLE/STALE_CSV: table=203 csv=40. The reflex is
&&   to import the CSV. That is backwards and destructive. Measured 2026-07-26:
&&
&&     SYSCMD_IMPORT_v2.csv holds 216 rows, and is NOT a superset of the live 203.
&&     Importing it would ADD 28 rows and SILENTLY LOSE 15:
&&       BUILDLMDB, PREDHELP, SETPATH, WHERECACHE, STUDENTECHO, STUDENTHELLO,
&&       and the nine SET compounds -- SET CASE, SET CDX, SET CNX, SET FILTER,
&&       SET INDEX, SET NEAR, SET ORDER, SET RELATION, SET UNIQUE.
&&
&&   Those 15 are deliberate maintainer entries. An earlier coverage generator
&&   read the 40-row CSV and reported 14.9% when the true figure against the
&&   table was 78.4%; acting on that number would have erased them.
&&
&&   The 28 rows v2 adds are a SEED GAP to be reviewed and appended one at a
&&   time. They are not applied here and this script cannot apply them.
&&
&& MUTATION
&&   Writes one file under DATA\tmp. Touches no table, no index, no LMDB.
&&   The caller decides whether the result is promoted over the tracked CSV.
&&
&& PATH PROTOCOL
&&   SETPATH DBF <dir>, then a BARE table name. Slashed relative paths resolve
&&   against the DATA root, not the DBF slot.
&&
&& Run:  ./datarun.ps1 -CommandLines 'DOTSCRIPT <abs path to this file>'

SET TALK OFF

; ===== SYSCMD EXPORT MIRROR START =====

SETPATH DBF metadata

WORKSPACE CLOSE
USE SYSCMD

; structure and count first -- the export is only meaningful against a known shape
FIELDS
COUNT

EXPORT TO tmp/SYSCMD_EXPORT_MIRROR_v1.csv CSV

; ===== SYSCMD EXPORT MIRROR END =====
QUIT
